+    Two layers, because the repo pins cards either way (#249: a container
+    pinned to one 3060 was described by a rig-wide 4×3090 sum):
+      1. docker inspect .HostConfig.DeviceRequests — what the RUNTIME handed
+         the container (device_ids / count: all). CDI runtimes ignore the env
+         masks, so this is the only truth there.
+      2. the container env's NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES / CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES —
+         the CUDA-level mask (`${ESTATE_GPUS:-...}`; launch.sh --gpus exports
+         UUIDs). When DeviceRequests says 'all' this mask narrows the scope to
+         what the engine can actually address.
+    Both known → intersection (empty → None). One known → it. Neither → None.
+    """
+    if not container:
+        return None
+    rig, by_uuid = _nvidia_gpu_inventory()
+    if not rig:
+        return None
+    dev, dev_all = _device_request_indices(container, rig, by_uuid)
+    env, env_all = _visible_devices_indices(container, rig, by_uuid)
+    if dev is None:
