+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# GPU-free regression section (#249 report, 2026-10-12):
+#   issue 1 — a --sweep died at the FIRST skipped cell: emit_row ran
+#     `python3 - <<'PY'`, whose heredoc IS stdin, so the JSON row piped in on
+#     the left was displaced by the program text; json.loads("") raised and
+#     set -e killed the sweep before any card / recommend / results file.
+#   issue 2 — VRAM and the GPU label were RIG-WIDE: vram_used_mb() summed every
+#     host GPU and _gpu_fp() named them all after GPU 0, so a 3060-pinned
+#     container on a 4×3090 rig reported 55 GB and "4× GeForce RTX 3090".
+#
+# Everything below needs no GPU and no docker: run_probe either runs against a
+# mock SSE server (real cells, the test-stream-toolcall-probe pattern) or is
+# stubbed at the python3 layer; nvidia-smi and docker are shimmed on PATH.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# 11. Negative control for the OLD emit_row shape: `python3 -` reads its
+#     PROGRAM from stdin, so piping the row in still leaves json.loads("")
+#     holding nothing. This must fail — if it ever passes, every assertion
+#     below is vacuous. (No file is created: 0 bytes written, like the report.)
+OLDROW="$(mktemp /tmp/cprobe-oldrow.XXXXXX)"
+set +e
+printf '%s\n' '{"ctx":32768,"n":8,"skip":"x"}' | python3 - "$OLDROW" <<'PY' 2>/dev/null
+import json, sys
+path = sys.argv[1]
+row = json.loads(sys.stdin.read())
+with open(path, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
+    fh.write(json.dumps(row, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
+PY
